     = note: each parameter's data lives in its own (generalized) region — the Cyclone default that
       keeps signatures annotation-free. A signature surface for declaring two parameters share
       a region is planned; today, `copy` the value into its container's region, or restructure
       so the allocation happens alongside the container.
     = note: this stores into a value declared outside the open `region` block. Such a store keeps
       nothing of the block when the stored value names no region (a scalar, a literal) or is
       written `copy e` at the store: that `copy` is a deep copy made in the outer value's
       region — the container's own for a `push`, an index or `Map` store or a `List`/`Map`
       replaced, the region ambient where the binding was declared for any other field
       [mem.region.outer-write].

